    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0458" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.61351/53</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Cuban Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">De Céspedes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 31, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In reply to your
                    excellency’s note in date of October 29, I have the honor to say that the Cuban
                    Sugar Commission will be glad to hold a conference with the International Sugar
                    Commission to discuss the question of the price of sugar as suggested by the
                    latter commission on Thursday, November 8.</p>
                <p>In view of the time of arrival of the trains, I beg to propose 3 p.m. as a
                    convenient hour at which the conference could be held.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
